  "worked_solution": "We are told that there are $18$ spherical beads in total. The tape diagram for those shows $3$ boxes. Therefore, each box in the diagram above represents $18÷3=6$ beads.  \n\nNow, we fill the number $6$ in each box of both tapes:\n\n![](/home/jake/Developer/Course_Academy/reference/mathacademy/capture/multivariable/14187307/assets/9b7efbe8e98fe498afbed34ffa33f02248eb72bd3a16a8683a5c26daefda9505.png)\n\nSince there are $5$ boxes corresponding to cubic beads, and each box represents $6$ beads, the number of the cubic beads is:\n\n$$\n5\\times 6=30\n$$\n\nSo, there are $30$ cubic beads in the necklace.",
